WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.668
[music playing]

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.907
It was find
everybody involved.

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:10.610
Find them now.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:12.779
We knew there was
an individual that

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:15.014
was responsible for all
the logistical movement

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:18.485
of marijuana and then cocaine,
but we weren't sure who he was.

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:24.921
So we raided house,
after house, after house.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.597
One name pops up, and
he continued to pop up--

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.250
Chapo Guzmán.

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:40.940
People called him
Chapo, which is a shorty.

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:27.487
He was a five-foot-six guy
who started out as a little

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:30.490
kid selling oranges on the side
of the road, down in Sinaloa.

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.967
At that time, he was
well down the ranks

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:42.202
of the Sinaloa cartel.

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:49.148
He was a border rat.

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:55.281
He knew virtually every
corner of the border--

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:59.819
where was the most
highly-patrolled area, where

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:05.225
were desolate areas, where was
the most valuable part of it

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:09.395
in terms of cocaine trafficking.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:14.300
Cartel bosses recognized
that he was extremely smart.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.536
He was years ahead
of anybody else

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:20.139
that ever came into the
drug-smuggling scene.

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:23.142
The flip side to
that is he was also

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:27.213
a ruthless, cold,
calculated killer.

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:36.923
30 guys were used to
dig this tunnel, night

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.725
and day, for months and months.

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:41.327
They kept them
locked up in a house.

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:44.898
And the cartel wanted to
keep it secret so bad,

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:47.600
and they were worried
somebody would talk about it,

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:51.941
so they executed them all
and dumped them into a well.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.880
So basically, all the
tunnel diggers dug

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:03.308
their own grave for the cartel.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.962
It was a gold mine for them.

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:21.935
A kilo of cocaine, back in those
days, about $24,000 a kilo.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:24.804
This tunnel probably
would have ran,

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:35.848
who knows, one truck a day,
two trucks a day, three maybe.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:43.556
Chapo went from the
little guy over here

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:47.994
in Douglas, to
captain in the cartel.

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:50.021
He was such a rising star.

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:02.208
Chapo was nicknamed
by the Colombians

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:03.943
as [speaking spanish]
because he was

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:07.463
so fast in moving the cocaine.

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:15.488
He didn't share his
methods of transportation,

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:21.394
but he was a genius
and troublemaker.

